                <pb facs="0806" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that the minister for foreign affairs has submitted the
                    case of the press boat <hi rendition="#italic">Hanyei Maru</hi> to the viceroy
                    by wire, and has asked again for reply to the request for permission for a
                    neutral vessel to take Japanese subjects from Korsakov.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
